# The assessment of AGT-003 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-003: "The validator shall reject out-of-scope files, undeclared dependency changes,
# missing tests/docs, malformed operations, unsupported tools, and unverifiable claims."
# Six named rejections.
#
# Two are real: `nomos-rules`' dependency-band judgment produces a finding for an edge that
# runs the wrong direction against declared bands (the nearest real site for 'undeclared
# dependency changes'), and `nomos-workspace`'s `WorkspaceError` refuses a structurally
# malformed change set outright ('malformed operations').
#
# A third, 'unverifiable claims', has an adjacent but opposite real site: `Commit`
# (`ValidatedPlan::Commit`, OD-CORRECTIONS-002) now requires an attached `Evidence` value,
# but that record states explicitly Commit "does not gate on the evidence's strength" -- an
# `AgentJudged`, i.e. unverifiable, claim is labelled honestly and still committed, not
# rejected.
#
# 'Out-of-scope files', 'missing tests/docs', and 'unsupported tools' have no real
# grounding: `CorrectionPlan::New` checks candidates only against each other for
# overlapping paths, never against any externally declared territory/scope, so nothing here
# would reject an out-of-scope file. `StagedPlan::Assert_Not_Stale` checks staleness and
# movement but nothing about test/doc presence or which tools produced an edit.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/rules/nomos-rules/src/checks/dependency/violations.rs#Violations_In
site: crates/substrate/nomos-workspace/src/workspace.rs#WorkspaceError
site: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/validated_plan.rs#Commit
gap: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/correction_plan.rs#New
gap: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/staged_plan.rs#Assert_Not_Stale
